WEBVTT

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.240
If even one of them loses,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.040
it'll give our opponents the right to challenge Tori.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.080
We have no choice but to believe

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.250
that everyone will protect those two!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.820
It is of Queen Anne.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.870
Wasn't Queen Anne the wife of Henry VIII

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.120
and the mother of the Fairy Queen Elizabeth?

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.290
Didn't she ultimately vanish like dew at the guillotine?

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.540
Judge! I'm amazed you knew about her.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.340
<i>I can't tell her that I learned that in an erotic game!</i>

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.420
Then, did you know this?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.100
Queen Catherine was supposed to give birth to Bloody Mary,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.220
but in actuality, she was unable to have children.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.810
Despite the need to reenact history,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.690
she was of frail constitution.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.560
So England came up with an excuse

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.230
to tell the Testament Union.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.240
They said Mary was hidden away by fairies.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.490
I-Is that the same as being spirited away?

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.950
Judge! It had even happened once before.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.120
Although they were only gone for a year,

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.080
there was an incident where three friends were hidden away by fairies.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.510
<i>Am I imagining things?</i>

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.730
<i>Why is her butt so round?</i>

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.860
<i>I am a boobs man, but with Master Scarred,</i>

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.320
<i>I may develop a thing for butts.</i>

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.570
You can see a most fascinating thing from here in the southwest tower.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.200
I already am!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.290
Eh?

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.460
Well, I mean you look great in that getup, Master Scarred!

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.420
Judge! Thank you.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.380
This was Henry VIII's study.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:04:00.260
Henry VIII was Tres España's previous Chancellor.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.640
Supposedly he was frequently compared to Carlos I,

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:07.600
who had concurrently served as emperor of the Holy Roman Empire.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.980
I have heard that Chancellor Carlos I
was a rather gifted man.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:17.150
According to the records, the two had shared exchanges.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.320
But when they met for the very first time,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.030
Henry VIII supposedly told Carlos I,

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.910
"Long time, my friend,"

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:28.540
which means, "It's been a long time, my friend."

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.880
M-Meaning that the two had already met?

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.090
A moment ago, I mentioned three people who were spirited away.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.390
They were Queen Catherine and Queen Anne before they succeeded to those names

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:45.680
and Henry VIII, who likewise had yet to succeed to that name.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.350
I don't know the details,

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.940
but apparently they attended the same school as Carlos I

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:54.230
when it happened.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.900
I see...

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.370
Master Tenzo, this is what I wanted to show you.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.160
Could this be related to the missing people

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.160
you are searching for?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:08.830
Wha—

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.750
Henry VIII became a Lost Noble?!

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.170
So, what's this say again?

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.380
Hm, I get it!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.880
Horizon!

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:24.390
Master Tori, you have experienced losing Horizon once before, yes?

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.810
I speculate that

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.020
you experienced the emotion "sadness" at that time.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.310
Is that correct?

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:31.690
Huh?

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:37.360
Emotions are stirred by various objects or living beings.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.320
It is safe to assume that they are linked with something or someone.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.950
Once that relationship is lost,

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.120
feelings of "sadness" come into existence.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.910
Master Tori, if you stay with me,

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:55.080
you will eventually lose me again and become sad.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.460
Even so, Master Tori,

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.920
you wish to form a relationship with me?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.470
The only ones not currently in this field are the following three:

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.930
Naruze, Masazumi and Mito.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.480
Fold your hands for Miss Honda's soul!

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.690
Huh? What's this?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.320
Oh, she's still deathly alive!

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.700
I'd've died instantly if I weren't in a guy's uniform!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.330
Damn it! How am I supposed to escape from this place?!

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.570
Here I go!

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.490
Go!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:10.990
Yes!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.800
<i>But she was busy confirming what was overhead!</i>

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.060
<i>Those are the lemons from that stall!</i>

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.030
You have a bazillion moves!

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.950
Tes. They are practical forms.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:54.250
<i>This woman's attacks had a one-in-two success rate,</i>

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.370
<i>but now each and every attack is coming straight at me!</i>

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:05.010
You're starting your attacks from your shoulders and elbows?

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.510
Tes. More accurately, these strikes are based on slashes and thrusts.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.720
This is the basis behind the greatest sword in the West!

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:23.610
Now!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.360
A shame cyanotics make for nasty mincemeat!

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.950
Oh, my. There's a banana peel.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.080
What say you, Sir Drake?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.330
Has the greatest in the West lost?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.800
Toussaint Neshinbara,

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:51.140
a war orphan from Tres España.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.930
You moved to Musashi before entering elementary school.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.100
During your second year of middle school,

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:59.350
you applied for the Testament Union-sponsored
Student Book Award.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.060
You received the Award for Excellence in the novelette category.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.230
During the interview at that time you said,

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.990
"This is the only occupation for me."

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:11.280
"I believe that receiving this award proves

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.330
that I am the type of person who can only become a writer."

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.170
But not only have you failed to release a book since then,

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.880
you haven't even been in a magazine.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:28.550
All you do is write fanzines and critiques.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.430
Tell me. Why did you stop writing?

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.720
And here you claimed that you couldn't become anything but a writer...

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.850
"Maybe I'll quit if it's too easy."

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.100
Is that what you thought?

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:45.730
You, me and that girl always said we'd do it.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.860
Don't you remember?

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:48.530
Huh?

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.030
It was back when we were still at that orphanage.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.950
When I grow up, I want to become a person who writes books.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.700
Me, too! That's what I want!

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.080
That again?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.120
What about you, Thirteen?

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.250
Of course I want to become a writer.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.340
No. That is the <i>only</i> thing I can become.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.590
Brimming with confidence, are we?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:14.340
Let's promise that someday

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.550
we'll have books lined up in bookstores.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.520
Yeah! The three of us will do it together!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:26.060
Yeah, we'll be in bookstores!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.740
I guess we did, huh?

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.580
That girl died.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:38.280
What?!

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:42.660
It was after you left, on our way to England.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.880
Which means that right now...

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:49.840
Can you tell which one I am?

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:00.810
There she is!

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:01.930
Naruze!

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.400
Arcabuz Cruz!

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:11.570
Stop right there!

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.910
Why did you stop me?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.080
There is no longer any need for you to fight.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:25.830
She's gone...

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.460
Damn it! If I could use spells...!

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.640
Hey, are you okay? Hang in there!

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.470
<i>I don't think he's dead, but he isn't moving.</i>

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.390
<i>What should I do?!</i>

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.560
Class 62-3, attention and death!

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:56.740
Miss Honda is gone.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:57.860
No death?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.830
What is this cushion?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.630
Thank goodness you're okay, Masazumi.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.210
Asama, are you all right?!

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.000
I am.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.510
I must have been standing

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.220
in front of you when we rescued you.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:17.050
Where is this?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.010
We're inside the barrier I made.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.310
More importantly, let me tend to him right away.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:25.640
Yeah... I'm so sorry.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.230
It's all my fault.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:34.190
Your mouse sent out an emergency signal due to that injury.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.530
That's what let me find your exact location.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:40.820
Be sure to tend to him and give him lots of love later.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.580
Thank you, Asama!

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:45.870
Thank goodness it wasn't a serious injury.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:50.040
Well, let's go to the city.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.920
Tori and Horizon are out that way.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.920
I imagine that is where everyone will gather up.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.920
Are they all okay?

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.180
Yes. Mito is the last one left.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.640
I managed to avoid taking a fatal blow, but...

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:07.810
Silver Chains!

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.690
Silver Chains?!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.030
Go, Gundog!

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.030
Two chains, release!

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.040
Silver Chains, wrap around me!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.410
Flat-Chested Evasion!

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:35.500
<i>Kimi and Asama couldn't slip through that!</i>

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.340
Silver Chains, embrace me and this doll with all your might!

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.640
<i>Goodness gracious...</i>

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.680
<i>If they don't properly wrap up that date,</i>

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.640
<i>I'm going to be quite upset.</i>

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.520
You just won that...

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:58.900
See, this'll get all grimy in a month or so

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.240
and you may wind up throwing it away someday.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:05.570
But you won't forget how I gave it to you or how you'd wear it.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.200
When you died all those years ago,

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.950
I came to realize something.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.620
Even with you gone, I'd think,

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.170
"Horizon probably would've said this."

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.540
"She probably would've done that."

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.800
Of course it's sad when you lose someone.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:27.550
But even so, the girl I knew was always with me.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.640
In other words, Master Tori,

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.940
you wish to fully memorize my action patterns

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:39.020
so that you can handle losing me at any given time?

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.280
That's not what I meant!

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.990
You don't do fun stuff to prepare for when you lose someone.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.120
If someone suddenly dies

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.240
even though you were having fun together,

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:50.120
you get cash back in the form of

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.660
reflecting on those good times.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.460
Is that so?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:15:00.130
But how do you obtain the emotion "fun"?

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.300
The Armaments of Deadly Sins

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.010
have only given me negative emotions.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:10.390
As such, even if we gather together all of the Deadly Weapons,

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.890
they will only give me negative emotions.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.850
They only create sadness.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:26.610
I don't... need that.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:31.580
Want some fried apples?

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.740
Judge.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.300
Are you sad right now?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:50.510
I am not sad.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:56.560
You know, not being sad is a joyous thing, Horizon.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.850
You have positive emotions.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:01.610
Why is that?

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:04.570
You were able to stop crying

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.530
because you fought against the sadness you felt.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.240
You mean to say that even if I obtain negative emotions,

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.290
I possess the positive emotions needed to resist them?

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:15.950
Yeah, you got it!

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.210
And your old man didn't die to bring you grief.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:25.170
He told us to gather your emotions to prevent the apocalypse.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.590
So you should build him a grave or something

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.680
and go look at that and mourn when you feel sad.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:34.350
After all, you've got a bunch of fun stuff

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:36.680
waiting for you once you take everything back.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.270
But is it right to take part in the world war

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:43.110
over my own selfish desires?

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:50.070
Yup! If you save even more people by gathering all of the Armaments of Deadly Sins...

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.530
That's when it'll be okay for you to join me in the war.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.620
I shall reserve making a decision.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.790
Master Tori, what about you?

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.090
I'm going to war.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:08.090
I want to see you become whole again.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.590
Even if that is not what I want?

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.140
Why not?

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:18.810
Even if you hate me once you get everything back,

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:21.100
it just means we're returning to the start line.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:25.860
I'll keep thinking about how much fun I've had as I move on.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:30.280
This is what I decided back when you died in front of me...

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.410
No... When I first met you!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:43.170
This is the best way for me to fend off my own sadness.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.420
Thank you.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.460
Huh?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.880
I will not say it again.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.550
I am an automated doll, after all.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.550
S-Seriously?

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.430
Everyone will be most pleased

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.310
that you have decided on what you intend to do.

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:02.020
Now then, let's go rescue them.

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:04.270
Huh? How?

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.440
Yikes!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.360
Isn't there a way?

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:10.320
C-Calm down, Horizon!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:13.990
I know! This'll be a snap for Asama and Big Sis!

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.910
Hey, Sis! Asama!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.200
You called?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.000
Sis!

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:24.210
The fields connected because you called for us.

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:28.670
Foolish Brother and adorable Horizon,

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:33.510
make sure to call for your genius sister should anything ever happen.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.260
Everything is related, isn't it?

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.180
You better prepare yourself, Horizon!

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.810
So? Were you able to discuss things?

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.680
With time to spare!

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:42.980
It was a breeze for me!
Really?

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.390
I shall wait to make a decision,

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.350
She won't say yet. Not yet! Not at this moment!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.860
but Master Tori has made his mind.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.690
<i>Air current! Jet current! Jet-black soy!</i>

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.730
Then no one fought in vain...

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.650
<i>Soy sauce! Soy sauce!</i>

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.900
...since he has decided what path Musashi will follow.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.780
Now what? What should I say next?

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.660
I'll say that!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.530
Let me know if you figure out which one I am.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:00.200
Will you forgive me if I guess right?

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:02.250
No.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.370
It would make her happy.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.300
Asama, have you connected with everyone?

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:19.350
I still haven't heard word from Adele, Suzu and Futayo.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.060
So close!

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.650
I did it!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.780
Rhythm games are fun, aren't they?

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.740
Think they're trying to force it open?

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:39.410
I-I know!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.450
Care to use this to learn what's happening outside?

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.080
Judge! This'll work!

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:49.630
Lemme borrow it.

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.510
Master Dudley, please wait just a moment longer!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.050
That's our queen for you!

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.680
To suggest we turn this mechanic shell into a shield!

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.140
Then I can open it with this darling!

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.850
Suzu, hang tight!

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:10.150
Master Dudley, the preparations are complete!

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:14.110
H-Here I go! Open up!

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.320
Go!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.960
That strange figure...

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:30.170
That is undoubtedly Master Adele's mechanic shell!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.260
She's headed toward the northwestern tower!

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.800
Fly, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.060
Master Tenzo, care to play a game?

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:46.810
What type of game?

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:50.100
How about one where I win

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:52.440
if I catch a glimpse of your face?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.320
Well, that'd be...

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.070
What was that?!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:08.160
Look out!

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.220
That was a close call.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:20.840
Thank you.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.970
My boy!

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:23.050
Mama!

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:27.310
Thank goodness they didn't get hurt.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:28.980
Are you okay, Master Scarred?

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:36.820
Thank goodness you did not get hurt!

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:39.690
<i>H-How scandalous! Keep it coming!</i>

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.030
Master... Scarred...?

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.080
Who are you?!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.250
You are not Master Scarred!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:52.830
You noticed?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.500
Where is this?

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.630
The execution grounds...?

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.720
Well, that isn't a problem.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.760
<i>I can't move! Is this spirit-based magic?</i>

00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:09.180
Is it you?

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.350
Are you the one who makes her promise falter?

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.230
The key to that decision...

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:22.740
<i>Why so serious</i>?!

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:27.910
Long time, my friend—no, my sister.

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:29.620
Isn't that right?

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:33.790
You're Double Bloody Mary, the one fated to be executed.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:34.710
Eh?!

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:42.550
Huh?

00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:44.840
What?!
